# Template for scripts/check-provenance.sh's local literal denylist.
#
# This repo is public. check-provenance.sh ships two tiers of pattern:
#   - STRUCTURAL patterns (ticket-ID formats, branch-naming conventions) live
#     inside the script itself — a naming FORMAT doesn't identify anyone, so
#     it's safe to publish.
#   - LITERAL patterns — an actual client name, an internal domain, a squad
#     name, a personal handle tied to one engagement — must never live in
#     tracked content. A denylist that ships its own literals in a public repo
#     publishes the very thing it exists to hide.
#
# Copy this file to .provenance-deny (already gitignored, never commit it) and
# fill in your own literals below, one extended-regex (grep -E) alternative
# per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# If .provenance-deny is absent, check-provenance.sh still runs — using only
# the structural patterns shipped in the script — and its OK/FAILED line
# always states whether a local file was loaded and how many patterns it
# contributed, so absence is visible in the gate's own output, never silent.
# A .provenance-deny that exists but yields zero usable lines is instead
# treated as an error (truncated/corrupted file), not as "nothing to hide".
#
# Examples only — replace with your own real values, don't ship these as-is:
# example-client-name
# example\.client\.domain
# \bExampleClientName\b
